     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""bin/memguard: unprivileged userspace memory watchdog for this shared VM (dec 021).
     3	
     4	Protects Etho (and the Claude sessions) from our own runaway work. No sudo, no systemd.
     5	Every --interval seconds (default 2):
     6	  1. Find TARGETS, only processes of our own uid that are either
     7	     (i)  carrying the bin/job env marker (GEMMA_JOB_CAP=... in /proc/<pid>/environ), i.e. bin/job
     8	          descendants, including orphans re-parented away from their wrapper; or
     9	     (ii) cwd under /home/ubuntu/work/gemma or /tmp, RSS > 3G, and comm not a session process
    10	          (claude/node/codex/tmux, or a bash/sh whose parent is one of those).
    11	     Nothing else is ever signalled. memguard's own job group is never a target.
    12	  2. Raise oom_score_adj to 1000 on every target (unprivileged), so the kernel picks us first.
    13	  3. Group targets into JOBS: a marked process's job root is its topmost marked ancestor; an
    14	     unmarked (ii) process is its own root. Job RSS = sum of targeted RSS in that tree.
    15	  4. If MemAvailable < --min-available (2.5G) or total targeted RSS > --max-total (6G), SIGKILL
    16	     the whole tree of the largest job: every descendant, then the root if still alive 3 s later
    17	     (so a bin/job wrapper gets to record "failed 137" first). Re-scan until there are no survivors.
    18	     Log to ops/logs/memguard.log, append to ops/jobs/<name>.log, and mail the builder.
    19	Reads only /proc/<pid>/{status,stat,environ,cwd,cmdline} of our own uid. Python stdlib only.
    20	Usage: bin/memguard [--once] [--dry-run] [--interval S] [--min-available G] [--max-total G]
    21	                    [--unmarked-rss G] [--marker NAME] [--roots DIR,DIR] [--log PATH] [--no-mail]
    22	"""
